mb|P|mb|1C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I not sure why East opened 1@C instead of 1@D unless you play short club, which we don't do at this table. A few players do play ^*BShort Club^*n meaning they only open 1@D with 4+. So if they are 4-4-3-2 they open 1@C. A 1@D opener only promises 3 in Standard American bidding.|
PG| ***** 1 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Another option could be discounting 1 for Qx in clubs and open 1N with a 15-17 points. But we will let 1@C stand.|
PG| ***** 2 ***** |


mb|P|mb|1S|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|mb|3S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Using |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenhandevaluation,Bergen Hand Evaluation^*N|CP||FP||at|, 3@S shows 4 spades and 17-19. East has 18 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=dummypoints,Bergen Dummy Points ^*N|CP||FP||at|--18 HCP, -1 for dubious Qx of clubs, + 1 for doubleton once fit is found. |

