nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So I will reluctantly pass. In response to a Kibitzer who suggested a double, I prefer 2@S to double with 5 spades, but double is possible. Obviously, I am going to be very unhappy if West raises to 3@H and the hand is passed out. Further, knowing we have around half of the deck, I would not be happy they are playing in 2@H in an 8 card fit either.|
PG| ***** 19 ***** |


mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 20 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
pc|CT|pc|C2|pc|CK|pc|CQ|
pg| ***** 21 ***** |


pc|SA|pc|S8|pc|S2|pc|S3|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now assuming partner defended correctly (which he did) because he led the @SA, I know he does not have the @SK. In the middle of the hand you lead K from AK on defense. So our only hope is to take 2 diamonds and hope for either a diamond ruff or 2 heart tricks.|
