qx|A4|st||rh||ah|Board 4 IMPs   -   April 24, 2024|pn|hondo717,IraCT,danpsych,aspiring|
md|2S4HQ2DQ98643CT983,SKT982HK963D2CJ52,SAHAT84DAKJT7CA64,SQJ7653HJ75D5CKQ7|sv|b|
mb|P|MB|2c|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|That is an interesting 2@C bid. Whenever you open a marginal 2@C bid, and your suit is a minor particularly diamonds you should think twice about opening 2@C because you are essentially preempting yourself. Moreover, your hand does not qualify for 2@C opener. Later please review my tutorial on how to  |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=open2c,open 2@C^*N|CP||FP||at|.|
PG| ***** 68 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|What I like to do with 20-21 and a singleton ace or king is open an imperfect 2N. Let me undo the bid.|
PG| ***** 69 ***** |


ub||
PG| ***** 70 ***** |


mb|2N|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In Match Points I would pass but in IMPs, with my 6 diamonds, we might be able to run diamonds. Further, and unless we can make exactly 2N, bidding 3N is only worth one undertrick at worst. So the upside in IMPs of making a game is worth the risk of stretching to bid 3N.|
PG| ***** 71 ***** |


mb|3N|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 72 ***** |


